minios-kernel-manager (1.2.2) unstable; urgency=high

  * Use minios-gui 1.1.0 shared HeaderBar and status banner components.
  * Discover and download real versioned kernel packages through the existing
    system APT configuration, using only temporary package workspaces.
  * Validate monolithic, Debian split, and Ubuntu split package ownership.
  * Produce compact format-1 registration metadata without embedding source
    package payloads in kernel bundles.
  * Preserve package control data, archive hashes, transformed payload hashes,
    and file ownership required for native dpkg registration.
  * Accept canonical tracked 01-kernel bundles and legacy 1.2.1 bundles during
    activation while keeping new Manager-produced bundles frozen.
  * Build initramfs from the selected extracted config and module tree, accept
    modular SquashFS support, and refuse ambiguous same-version module trees.

 -- crims0n <crims0n@minios.dev>  Wed, 12 Aug 2026 01:00:00 +0300

minios-kernel-manager (1.2.1) unstable; urgency=high

  * Adopt python3-minios-gui 1.0.0 for shared styling, icons, dialogs, row
    sizing, status accents, and bounded log output.
  * Confine privileged package construction to private workspaces and reject
    symlinked or mismatched kernel artifacts.
  * Refuse deletion of active, running, or symlinked kernel repository entries.
  * Roll back boot files, bootloader configuration, and the active marker as one
    activation transaction, and accept only an identical retained repository
    copy during subsequent kernel switches.
  * Verify the actual mksquashfs compressor and the target kernel's built-in
    SquashFS decoder before publishing a kernel bundle.
  * Emit typed one-line NDJSON records with nonzero status on failed mutations.
  * Use shared manager row sizing and active-first status accents consistent
    with Session Manager.
  * Restore Python 3.6 and pytest 3.3 compatibility in the source test suite.

 -- crims0n <crims0n@minios.dev>  Mon, 10 Aug 2026 00:29:10 +0300

minios-kernel-manager (1.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Preserve encrypted-persistence support when rebuilding kernels and reject
    replacements without the required initramfs crypto capability.
  * Confine kernel repository and bootloader updates against path traversal and
    symlink escapes, write active files atomically, and roll back failed
    activation.
  * Fail packaging when repository installation fails and retain kernel package
    dpkg metadata in generated SquashFS images.
  * Improve repository discovery and refresh by filtering duplicate and
    non-versioned kernel packages and using APT list freshness.
  * Handle MiniOS mount paths containing spaces and improve cancellation and
    stale-result handling for GUI package operations.
  * Refresh the interface with the compact MiniOS HeaderBar, status banners,
    framed content, theme-aware colors, and consistent footer spacing.

 -- crims0n <crims0n@minios.dev>  Sun, 19 Jul 2026 01:20:44 +0300

